    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "**Owner iPhone Safari acceptance: PARTIAL PASS; ONE remaining scoped UX defect on exact PR HEAD `af016d7ee57285ef3c87c1a2285b305354598c7a` (2026-10-31). Keep OPEN/DRAFT/UNMERGED.**\n\nAll other UI behavior checked by owner is **PASS**. Do not reopen already accepted compact topbar, native keyboard/focus, DM message list and composer, report suggestion list, report artifact fix, or tabs/swipes. The **remaining issue** is wasted empty space in the lower mobile panel across *all three empty-tab cases*:\n\n- **Battles 0:** the \"пошли в баттл\" CTA and \"Раундов нет.\" are at top, but #battlesBody/panel expands down to viewport bottom with huge blank area.\n- **Events 0:** one \"Движ пока спит.\" message sits above a massive empty gradient pane.\n- **DM 0:** correct empty-state copy (\"Личных переписок пока нет\"; \"Чтобы начать, нажмите на имя игрока в общем чате.\") is vertically centered in a huge panel.\n\n**Desired behavior:** each empty tab remains **content-height / compact**, with a short inline empty-state label and any legitimate CTA. Give recovered vertical space back to **general chat**, making it the dominant, usable pane while the selected lower tab has no content. Keep the tabs themselves visible and touchable, and keep the user-selected chat height for later restoration. No invented battle/event/DM data. When actual DM, battle or event content arrives or the user switches tabs, restore full-height content-capable panel smoothly; preserve current DM priority for **populated DM**. Respect physical iOS keyboard and `visualViewport`, safe areas and manual resize.\n\n**Confirmed code-level reason to investigate:** mobile `AsyncScene/Web/ui/mobile-ui.css` sets `#mobilePanelShell` to the remaining viewport height and `#blocks > .panel:not(#menuBlock){height:100%;flex:1 1 100%}`; `ui-core.js` computes `--mobile-panels-height` as **all** remaining space, irrespective of active-tab emptiness. `style-base.css` centers `#dmLog.dmEmptyState` inside the flexed 100%-height panel. Fix the sizing/data-state at the layout ownership level, not merely by moving the empty text. Do not casually edit `ui/mobile-ui.css`, which is **outside the existing eight approved PR paths**; if editing is truly required, explicitly request a narrow owner/lock authorization first (and mirror in docs).\n\n**Tests**: real-empty state for DM/Battles/Events on small and large iPhones; button remains clickable, no huge blank lower panel; chat gains the space and composer stays visible; populated-to-empty and empty-to-populated transitions, switching tabs, chat drag/restore, keyboard and Safari visualViewport, scrolling; desktop unchanged; all already PASS functions unchanged. Include DOM rect dimensions, not screenshot-only heuristics. Run browser seven sizes, Python, Node, `git diff --check`, Web/docs parity and independent exact-head review. Publish only to existing PR #431, normal child commit, no merge or deploy. After publication, owner must retest Safari on exact SHA.\n\nOwner provided **three annotated screenshots** (Battles 0, Events 0, DM 0) in the conversation. New Codex executor must request/use those attachments; they are not automatically attached to this GitHub comment. **Scope is only compact empty mobile panels**, all else is accepted.",
